    <div class="alpheios-lex-entry" lemma-id="n32034" root="غطرف" body-key="g">
    
      Q. 2 
      <b><span class="alpheios-lex-ar" lang="ara">تَغَطْرَفَ</span></b>  <i>He sought chiefdom,</i> or <i>lordship;</i>
[&amp;c.;] from <span class="alpheios-lex-ar" lang="ara">غِطْرِيفٌ</span> meaning <span class="alpheios-lex-ar" lang="ara">سَيِّدٌ</span>. (O.) ― 
       <p class="alpheios-lex-sense-separator"> </p><span class="alpheios-lex-sense-spacer2"> </span>-b2-  And
<i>He magnified himself,</i> or <i>was proud:</i> (El-Ahmar,
O, K:) [and so, app., ↓ <b><span class="alpheios-lex-ar" lang="ara">غَطْرَفَ</span></b> , for] <span class="alpheios-lex-ar" lang="ara">غَطْرَفَةٌ</span> and
<span class="alpheios-lex-ar" lang="ara">تَغَطْرُفٌ</span> and <span class="alpheios-lex-ar" lang="ara">تَغَتْرُفٌ</span> signify <span class="alpheios-lex-ar" lang="ara">تَكَبُّرٌ</span>: (S:) [or] <i>he was
proud, haughty,</i> or <i>self-conceited, in walk</i> (IAar,
O, K) especially. (IAar, O)

